※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4922 LANG_OPERATOR_ARITY

※ A pair is written around what it is applied to, so it takes that and at least
※ one thing to stand inside: a definition of one parameter would be a pair with
※ nothing between the brackets, which is not what brackets are for.

type Grid = a : u8 ; b : u8

fn `⟬⟭`(g: Grid) → u8:
    g.a

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
